1
00:00:00,475 --> 00:00:03,339
Welcome to AIB Life's service governance application.

2
00:00:03,349 --> 00:00:06,702
Follow the complete journey, from operational data sources to a clear,

3
00:00:06,712 --> 00:00:08,810
evidence based view of performance.

4
00:00:09,517 --> 00:00:13,223
Upload your data sources, apply the Schedule twenty three rules, investigate

5
00:00:13,233 --> 00:00:16,014
the results, and share a monthly governance pack.

6
00:00:16,024 --> 00:00:18,017
Here is how the journey connects.

7
00:00:18,725 --> 00:00:21,251
The dashboard brings reporting periods together.

8
00:00:21,261 --> 00:00:24,561
See which service levels missed target, how many policies were measured,

9
00:00:24,571 --> 00:00:26,154
and what remains overdue.

10
00:00:26,164 --> 00:00:28,729
A shortcut opens the latest governance pack.

11
00:00:29,433 --> 00:00:31,174
Start in Data Sources.

12
00:00:31,184 --> 00:00:34,428
Upload correspondence, cancellation, withdrawal, and workflow files as

13
00:00:34,438 --> 00:00:36,013
CSV or Excel.

14
00:00:36,023 --> 00:00:39,140
The application identifies each source from its contents.

15
00:00:39,850 --> 00:00:42,662
The checklist confirms all five required sources.

16
00:00:42,672 --> 00:00:45,040
File details show the records received.

17
00:00:45,050 --> 00:00:47,967
The snapshot date and quality notes explain the evidence behind the reporting

18
00:00:47,977 --> 00:00:49,004
set.

19
00:00:49,725 --> 00:00:52,465
New files replace earlier files in the same slot and rebuild every

20
00:00:52,475 --> 00:00:53,735
monthly pack.

21
00:00:53,745 --> 00:00:57,011
Analysts can also rebuild on demand, remove files, or reload the supplied

22
00:00:57,021 --> 00:00:58,432
data sources.

23
00:00:59,142 --> 00:01:01,348
Choose a reporting month from the dashboard.

24
00:01:01,358 --> 00:01:03,806
Search makes older periods easy to find.

25
00:01:03,816 --> 00:01:07,898
Incomplete periods are clearly labelled, keeping partial months in context.

26
00:01:08,642 --> 00:01:11,889
Reports provides access to SLA Status, exceptions, and the governance

27
00:01:11,899 --> 00:01:12,836
pack.

28
00:01:12,846 --> 00:01:16,371
Status compares five headline service levels against target, with met,

29
00:01:16,381 --> 00:01:18,559
missed, and overdue counts.

30
00:01:19,267 --> 00:01:23,311
Pass or fail uses completed policies: met divided by met plus missed.

31
00:01:23,321 --> 00:01:25,696
The second rate includes overdue open work.

32
00:01:25,706 --> 00:01:29,732
Counts represent service records, so a policy can appear more than once.

33
00:01:30,433 --> 00:01:33,373
Select a service level to see its underlying policies.

34
00:01:33,383 --> 00:01:36,611
Product, handler, timing, and outcome connect each result to operational

35
00:01:36,621 --> 00:01:37,663
evidence.

36
00:01:37,673 --> 00:01:41,162
Unit linked performance also expands into three component steps.

37
00:01:41,892 --> 00:01:44,252
Outcome filters narrow the list immediately.

38
00:01:44,262 --> 00:01:46,999
Isolate missed policies and compare the required deadline with actual

39
00:01:47,009 --> 00:01:50,396
completion, using the evidence that produced the monthly score.

40
00:01:51,100 --> 00:01:54,558
Exceptions brings failing service levels and failed policies together.

41
00:01:54,568 --> 00:01:57,383
Switch between missed deadlines and open overdue work.

42
00:01:57,393 --> 00:02:01,228
A service level can pass overall and still contain individual exceptions.

43
00:02:01,933 --> 00:02:05,647
Data quality findings flag overdue policies, unmatched approvals, exclusions,

44
00:02:05,657 --> 00:02:07,326
and incomplete periods.

45
00:02:07,336 --> 00:02:11,009
Reviewers can see where the evidence needs attention before drawing conclusions.

46
00:02:11,725 --> 00:02:14,353
Open Intelligence to explore the reporting history.

47
00:02:14,363 --> 00:02:17,726
The latest complete month's status sits alongside recurring misses, performance

48
00:02:17,736 --> 00:02:21,071
trends, and outstanding work across the reporting window.

49
00:02:21,808 --> 00:02:25,950
Amazon Nova Pro turns the computed report figures into an executive explanation.

50
00:02:25,960 --> 00:02:29,226
The summary covers recent performance, the wider reporting window, failure

51
00:02:29,236 --> 00:02:31,789
concentrations, and overdue backlog.

52
00:02:32,517 --> 00:02:35,862
Monthly trends compare each service level with its target over time.

53
00:02:35,872 --> 00:02:38,383
Change the selection to explore another pattern.

54
00:02:38,393 --> 00:02:41,795
The service level record summarises complete months below target.

55
00:02:42,517 --> 00:02:45,201
The scope selector narrows the analysis to a chosen month and everything

56
00:02:45,211 --> 00:02:46,245
before it.

57
00:02:46,255 --> 00:02:49,055
The executive summary refreshes for that window, keeping the governance

58
00:02:49,065 --> 00:02:50,660
discussion focused.

59
00:02:51,392 --> 00:02:54,823
Failure concentrations highlight handlers, products, and transaction types

60
00:02:54,833 --> 00:02:56,912
with unusually high failure rates.

61
00:02:56,922 --> 00:02:59,069
These patterns direct investigation.

62
00:02:59,079 --> 00:03:02,293
They show where failures occur, without proving their cause.

63
00:03:03,017 --> 00:03:05,937
The backlog groups open overdue policies by service level and shows the

64
00:03:05,947 --> 00:03:07,331
oldest deadline.

65
00:03:07,341 --> 00:03:10,303
This keeps unfinished obligations visible alongside the formal completed

66
00:03:10,313 --> 00:03:12,134
policy performance rate.

67
00:03:12,850 --> 00:03:14,809
Ask a question about the report.

68
00:03:14,819 --> 00:03:18,423
Here, Nova explains where non unit linked failures concentrate.

69
00:03:18,433 --> 00:03:21,357
The model's answer uses the report's computed evidence, with its source

70
00:03:21,367 --> 00:03:23,417
identified beneath the response.

71
00:03:24,142 --> 00:03:26,931
Open Governance pack directly from the month's results.

72
00:03:26,941 --> 00:03:30,207
The dashboard also offers a shortcut to the latest complete month.

73
00:03:30,217 --> 00:03:34,122
Summary, SLA Status, exceptions, quality findings, and source evidence

74
00:03:34,132 --> 00:03:35,697
form one document.

75
00:03:36,433 --> 00:03:39,756
Select Export as PDF, then choose Save as PDF in the browser's

76
00:03:39,766 --> 00:03:40,951
print window.

77
00:03:40,961 --> 00:03:43,938
Share the monthly findings with colleagues and clients, supported by the

78
00:03:43,948 --> 00:03:46,031
evidence reviewed throughout this journey.

79
00:03:46,767 --> 00:03:49,650
From five data sources to a traceable governance story.

80
00:03:49,660 --> 00:03:52,588
Prepare the evidence, review performance, investigate exceptions, and

81
00:03:52,598 --> 00:03:54,057
share the findings.

82
00:03:54,067 --> 00:03:56,849
AIB Life, with clarity at every step.
